### Scenario A: Register Alice as a Manager
POST {{Hostname}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@company.com",
  "password": "Alice@2026!",
  "role": "Manager"
}

### Scenario B: Register Bob as an Employee
POST {{Hostname}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "email": "bob@company.com",
  "password": "Bob@2026!",
  "role": "Employee"
}

### Scenario C: Login as Alice
POST {{Hostname}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Alice@2026!"
}

### Scenario D: Manager Accesses Team Reports (Policy Authorization)
GET {{Hostname}}/api/reports/team-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{AliceToken}}

### Scenario E: Unauthenticated Access Attempt
GET {{Hostname}}/api/reports/team-summary

### Scenario F: Retrieve Alice's Own Tasks
GET {{Hostname}}/api/tasks/my
Authorization: Bearer {{AliceToken}}
### Scenario G: Login as Bob (To get an Employee Token)
POST {{Hostname}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "Bob@2026!"
}

### Scenario H: Employee Accessing Manager Reports (Should return 403 Forbidden)
// Copy Bob's token from the response above and temporarily replace the variable below if testing manually
@BobToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..ACiPxPZtevsBdFclHZaSr2nwIxxFofJcgBT_a0FPFOE
